# Myriad (CR 702.116a): Wyrm's Crossing Patrol (1/1) attacks Bot2, so for each opponent other than the defending player - Bot3 - Bot1
# may create a token copy tapped and attacking that player. It chooses Bot3: a tapped 1/1 copy attacking Bot3 while the
# Patrol attacks Bot2. The token was never declared as an attacker, so its own myriad does not trigger (no second token, and no
# question about Bot2). Both opponents take 1 in combat, and the token is exiled at end of combat. Mox Pearl pays for the Patrol.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Wyrm's Crossing Patrol
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[T4 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 2
? Combat.Attackers = Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2; Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol#2.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol#2.Token = true
[T4 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot3.Life = 19
? Delayed.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol.Tapped = true
Exile.Count = 0
